# Phosphor Icons

**Trigger**: Auto-applied to all `.tsx` and `.ts` files importing from `@phosphor-icons/react`.

## Package

- **Version**: `@phosphor-icons/react` v2.1.10 (May 2025)
- **Source**: [phosphoricons.com](https://phosphoricons.com) | [GitHub](https://github.com/phosphor-icons/react)
- **Already in `package.json`** — do not reinstall.

## Import Paths (Critical)

The package has **three import paths**. Using the wrong one causes SSR/hydration errors.

| Context | Import Path | Why |
|---------|-------------|-----|
| **Server Component** (no `"use client"`) | `@phosphor-icons/react/ssr` | SSR-safe; no React Context dependency |
| **Client Component** (has `"use client"`) | `@phosphor-icons/react` | Full features; supports `IconContext` |
| **Shadcn UI component files** | `@phosphor-icons/react` | UI components are client-side |

### SSR vs CSR — The Rule

```tsx
// ✅ SERVER COMPONENT — use /ssr subpath
// File: app/(dashboard)/dashboard/page.tsx  (no "use client")
import { Sparkle, TrendUp } from "@phosphor-icons/react/ssr";

// ✅ CLIENT COMPONENT — use main entry
// File: components/dashboard/ai-insights-card.tsx  (has "use client")
import { Sparkle, TrendUp } from "@phosphor-icons/react";

// ✅ SHADCN UI FILE — use main entry (these are always client-side)
// File: components/ui/dialog.tsx
import { XIcon } from "@phosphor-icons/react";

// ❌ NEVER use dist/ssr directly
import { FishIcon } from "@phosphor-icons/react/dist/ssr";

// ❌ NEVER use CSR import in a Server Component (causes hydration error)
// File: app/(dashboard)/dashboard/page.tsx
import { Sparkle } from "@phosphor-icons/react";
```

### Decision Checklist

1. Does the file have `"use client"` at the top? → Use `@phosphor-icons/react`
2. Is the file a Shadcn UI component in `components/ui/`? → Use `@phosphor-icons/react`
3. Otherwise (Server Component, page, layout)? → Use `@phosphor-icons/react/ssr`

## Icon Naming Convention

### Exported Names

Phosphor exports icons with **`Icon` suffix**. Always include the suffix.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT — Icon suffix
import { HeartIcon, Sparkle, ArrowRight } from "@phosphor-icons/react/ssr";

// Both forms are exported (with and without Icon suffix).
// Prefer the Icon suffix for clarity and consistency.
import { SparkleIcon, ArrowRightIcon } from "@phosphor-icons/react/ssr";
```

### Type Import

When typing icon props or variables, import the `Icon` type from the **main entry** (not `/ssr`):

```tsx
import type { Icon } from "@phosphor-icons/react";

const MyIcon: Icon = Sparkle;
```

## Props and Styling

Icon components accept all standard SVG props plus Phosphor-specific props:

| Prop | Type | Default | Usage |
|------|------|---------|-------|
| `size` | `number \| string` | `"1em"` | Height & width. Use Tailwind via `className="size-4"` |
| `weight` | `"thin" \| "light" \| "regular" \| "bold" \| "fill" \| "duotone"` | `"regular"` | Icon style weight |
| `color` | `string` | `"currentColor"` | Stroke/fill color. Use CSS variable tokens |
| `mirrored` | `boolean` | `false` | Flip horizontally (RTL support) |
| `alt` | `string` | — | Accessible alt text |

### Styling via Tailwind

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — Tailwind classes
<SparkleIcon className="size-4 text-muted-foreground" weight="regular" />

// ❌ BAD — inline styles for size/color
<SparkleIcon style={{ width: 16, height: 16, color: '#888' }} />
```

### Color Tokens

Use semantic CSS variables, not hardcoded hex values:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — semantic token
<CheckCircleIcon className="size-4 text-success" />

// ❌ BAD — hardcoded
<CheckCircleIcon className="size-4" color="#22c55e" />
```

## Dynamic Icon Patterns

When mapping icon names to components dynamically, import from the correct path and use a lookup:

```tsx
// Server component pattern
import { House, PencilSimple, Calendar } from "@phosphor-icons/react/ssr";
import type { Icon } from "@phosphor-icons/react";

function getIcon(name: string): Icon {
  switch (name) {
    case "house": return House;
    case "pencil-simple": return PencilSimple;
    case "calendar": return Calendar;
  }
}

// Usage
const IconComponent = getIcon(item.icon);
<IconComponent className="size-4" weight="regular" />
```

## Next.js Configuration

**Do NOT add `@phosphor-icons/react` to `serverExternalPackages`**. This causes SSR errors because Node.js cannot correctly resolve the `/ssr` export path when the package is external.

The package has `sideEffects: false` in its package.json, so tree-shaking works correctly when bundled by Next.js. Only the icons you actually import will be included in the bundle.

```tsx
// next.config.ts — DO NOT add @phosphor-icons/react to serverExternalPackages
const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
  // serverExternalPackages should NOT include "@phosphor-icons/react"
  // The package handles SSR exports correctly when bundled
};
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Fix |
|-------------|---------|-----|
| `import from "@phosphor-icons/react/dist/ssr"` | Non-standard path, may break in updates | Use `@phosphor-icons/react/ssr` |
| CSR import in Server Component | Hydration mismatch, Context API unavailable in RSC | Use `/ssr` subpath |
| SSR import in Client Component | Loses `IconContext` support | Use main entry |
| Hardcoded `color` hex values | Breaks theme/dark mode | Use Tailwind color tokens |
| Inline `style` for size | Ignores Tailwind scale | Use `className="size-N"` |
| Importing all icons via `import * as Icon` | Prevents tree-shaking, bloats bundle | Import individual icons |
| Missing `Icon` suffix on names | Inconsistent naming | Use `SparkleIcon` not `Sparkle` |

## Verification

Before committing changes involving phosphor-icons:

- [ ] Server components import from `@phosphor-icons/react/ssr`
- [ ] Client components import from `@phosphor-icons/react`
- [ ] Shadcn UI components import from `@phosphor-icons/react`
- [ ] No imports from `@phosphor-icons/react/dist/*`
- [ ] No hardcoded hex/rgb colors on icon `color` prop
- [ ] Icon sizes use Tailwind `className="size-N"` pattern
- [ ] `pnpm run build` passes (no hydration errors)
